#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""orig: run and drive the original NFS Most Wanted (2012) automatically, for research.

The game runs inside gamescope (a nested display, headless by default): it always has focus, input goes in
through that display only (never the desktop), and screenshots come from gamescope. Car state is read from the
game's memory with the same watch file as `mwtool telemetry` (read-only).

One-time setup:  tools/orig/orig setup        (prints the Steam launch option to set)
Typical use:
    tools/orig/orig launch                     # start the game in headless gamescope, wait for its window
    tools/orig/orig shot menu.png              # screenshot (look at it, decide the next input)
    tools/orig/orig key Return                 # tap a key; also: hold w 3, type, click x y
    tools/orig/orig read speed_mph gear        # values from handling.watch
    tools/orig/orig run script.orig            # a script of steps (see `orig run --help`)
    tools/orig/orig quit
`orig run-in -- <command>` runs any program the same way (used to test the tool on Most Rusted itself).

Everything is read-only towards the game's files and code: inputs are synthetic key / pad events, memory is
only read. Keep the game offline.

`orig launch --probe` additionally loads the probe DLL (crates/mw-probe, docs/probe.md) into the game for that
run only: the built DLL is copied next to NFS13.exe under the name of a system DLL the game loads
(--proxy, default xinput1_3), that name is overridden to "native" through WINEDLLOVERRIDES, and MW_PROBE_OUT
names the directory it logs into (ref/probe/<name>/). `orig quit` (and the next `launch`) removes the copy.
`orig modules` lists the DLLs the running game has loaded, to choose the proxy name.

Input notes (2026-10-04, the 1.4 Steam build under Proton):
- Keyboard events reach the game only after `activate()` (sent automatically): headless gamescope never sends
  WM_TAKE_FOCUS, and Wine ignores keys for a window it does not consider active.
- Menus take keys any time; driving reads the device chosen in Settings > Gameplay > Controller. With
  "Keyboard": Left / Right steer, A accelerate, Z brake, Space handbrake. With the pad: left stick, RT, LT, X.
- The virtual pad (uinput) is not seen while Steam Input is on for the game (Steam only picks controllers up
  through hidraw); select "Keyboard" in the game for automated driving, and switch it back afterwards.
"""

